message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "grounding-atlas: a pilot benchmark of supervised biological decodability and native model output"
abstract: >-
  A pilot research benchmark comparing native model outputs with supervised
  representation-label readouts across biological and scientific representations.
  GroundBench records operational target definitions, task status, truth level,
  paired entity identifiers, raw outputs, parse validity, proper scores, and
  provenance metadata. A supervised decodability-native-output gap is an operational
  statistical contrast; it does not by itself establish latent biological knowledge,
  causal use of a decoded feature, a specialist ceiling, or a universal law.
type: software
